Z||000000||Viper'sVenom||09-18-2001||10:16 AM||||I am curious if it is possible to have a supercharged engine in a fiero.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sootah||09-18-2001||10:58 AM||||They drop SC 3800's in all the time. As far as I know its the most common engine swap. As for a SC V8, I don't know.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">   <BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I> <BR><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter||||reg||2
Z||000002||KissMySSFiero||09-18-2001||01:56 PM||||if your talking about a blower on top of the engine i doubt it could be done.  just not enough room to run a belt to it.  now if youre talking about the kind that you bolt on to the side of the engine and run a belt to that(like where the AC comp is)  then  it may be able to be done but i doubt that too.  there just isnt enough room in a fiero.  i have heard rumors of turboed v8 fieros but never seen such a thing.  again no room.  if you want to do it just to have the only one the be prepared to spend a lot of $$$$$.  if you want it just to be fast then i say build a hot motor and run NOS.  i see no reason why a small block cant put out 450-500 horses in a fiero.  but even then you wont have much reliability.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000003||DreXteR||09-18-2001||02:50 PM||||It can be done. You will need a centrifugal sc. Those like vortech. But first document your self.<P>DreX<p>[This message has been edited by DreXteR (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||09-18-2001||03:02 PM||||Maybe with the Zumalt kit you can have the space. Still a lot of fabrication and $$$!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Turbo88||09-18-2001||03:40 PM||||You will have a tough time fitting a centrifugal supercharger too. I turbo will allow you to put the power adder in a more convienient location but it will be a pain in the ass to route the exhaust and intake routing would be an act of God if your engine has a forward mounted throttlebody (like the LT1 and LS1).<P>||||reg||1
